+## Creating a JSON Patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` returns the JSON Patch ([RFC 6902](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)) that turns `from`
+into `to` when applied with `applyPatch`. The patch describes what changed and nothing more: a change to one member
+or one array element is one operation, and an element inserted or removed in the middle of an array is one operation
+too. Equal documents give an empty patch. The inputs are not modified.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from './src/index.ts';
+
+createPatch({ title: 'Hello', tags: ['a', 'c'] }, { title: 'Hello', tags: ['a', 'b', 'c'] });
+// [{ op: 'add', path: '/tags/1', value: 'b' }]
+```
+
+It throws a `SyntaxError` when `from` or `to` contains a value that is not a JSON value. Patches are not always
+minimal: a reordered array, or several scattered changes within one array, may take more operations than strictly
+needed, but the patch is always correct.
+
